    turnFlow: "1. **Bidding (Otea)**: Dealer's opponents place one card face-up. This signifies their desire for that suit to be trumps. 2. **Trump Flip**: Dealer turns up the top card of the stock. This suit becomes trump. If an opponent bid that suit, they swap their bid card for the trump card. 3. **The Play**: Lead any card. Others play any card (no follow-suit requirement). 4. **Winning**: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest card of the led suit wins. 5. **Drawing**: Winner 'eats' the trick, draws a new card from the stock first, then others draw. Lead next. 6. **Endings**: Play continues until stock and hands are empty.",
